Appendix G: Particle Filter Derivations

G.1 Bayesian Filtering for Hybrid Systems

The state-space model is:

X_t \sim p(X_t \mid X_{t-1}) \quad \text{(transition)}


\mathbf{y}_t \sim p(\mathbf{y}_t \mid X_t) \quad \text{(observation)}

The filtering distribution $p(X_t \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t})$ satisfies the recursion:

Prediction:
p(X_t \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t-1}) = \int p(X_t \mid X_{t-1}) p(X_{t-1} \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t-1}) dX_{t-1}

Update:
p(X_t \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t}) = \frac{p(\mathbf{y}_t \mid X_t) p(X_t \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t-1})}{\int p(\mathbf{y}_t \mid X_t') p(X_t' \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t-1}) dX_t'}

G.2 Interacting Multiple Model (IMM) Particle Filter

For a hybrid system with discrete modes $q \in \mathcal{Q}$ and continuous state $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^r$, the IMM approximates the posterior as:

p(\mathbf{x}_t, q_t \mid \mathbf{y}_{1:t}) \approx \sum_{i=1}^N w_t^{(i)} \delta_{\mathbf{x}_t^{(i)}}(\mathbf{x}_t) \delta_{q_t^{(i)}}(q_t)

Algorithm G.1 (IMM Particle Filter).

1. Initialization: For $i = 1,\dots,N$:
   · Sample $q_0^{(i)} \sim \pi_0$
   · Sample $\mathbf{x}_0^{(i)} \sim p_0(\mathbf{x} \mid q_0^{(i)})$
   · Set $w_0^{(i)} = 1/N$
2. For $t = 1, 2, \dots$:
   a. Mode-Conditioned Prediction: For each particle $i$ and each possible new mode $q' \in \mathcal{Q}$:
   · Compute mixing probability: $\mu^{(i)}(q') = P(q_t = q' \mid q_{t-1} = q_{t-1}^{(i)}, \mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{(i)})$
   · Propagate state: $\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_t^{(i,q')} = \Phi_{q'}(\mathbf{x}_{t-1}^{(i)}, \Delta t) + \boldsymbol{\epsilon}^{(i,q')}$, $\boldsymbol{\epsilon} \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \mathbf{Q}_{q'})$
   b. Weight Update:
   · Compute likelihood: $L^{(i,q')} = \mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y}_t; \mathbf{h}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_t^{(i,q')}, q'), \boldsymbol{\Sigma})$
   · Unnormalized weight: $\tilde{w}_t^{(i,q')} = w_{t-1}^{(i)} \cdot \mu^{(i)}(q') \cdot L^{(i,q')}$
   c. Resampling:
   · Normalize weights: $w_t^{(i,q')} = \tilde{w}_t^{(i,q')} / \sum_{i,q'} \tilde{w}_t^{(i,q')}$
   · Resample $N$ particles with replacement from the weighted set $\{(\tilde{\mathbf{x}}_t^{(i,q')}, q'), w_t^{(i,q')}\}$
   d. Mode Mixing (IMM Step):
   · For each resampled particle, apply IMM mixing to prevent sample impoverishment:
   · Compute mode probabilities $\pi_t(q) = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i: q_t^{(i)} = q} 1$
   · For particles with $q_t^{(i)} = q$, blend their continuous states with those from other modes according to the transition probabilities.
   e. Age Update:
   · For each particle: if $q_t^{(i)} = q_{t-1}^{(i)}$, $a_t^{(i)} = a_{t-1}^{(i)} + \Delta t$; else $a_t^{(i)} = 0$.
3. Output: State estimate $\hat{\mathbf{x}}_t = \sum_i w_t^{(i)} \mathbf{x}_t^{(i)}$, mode estimate $\hat{q}_t = \arg\max_q \sum_{i: q_t^{(i)}=q} w_t^{(i)}$.

G.3 Sequential Monte Carlo Squared (SMC²)

When $\boldsymbol{\theta}$ is unknown, SMC² [A17] performs Bayesian inference on the joint space of parameters and states.

Algorithm G.2 (SMC² for PDMP).

1. Initialization: Sample $M$ parameter particles $\boldsymbol{\theta}^{(m)} \sim p(\boldsymbol{\theta})$, $m = 1,\dots,M$.
2. For each SMC² iteration $k = 1, 2, \dots$:
   a. State Particle Filter: For each $\boldsymbol{\theta}^{(m)}$, run Algorithm G.1 on the full dataset $\mathbf{y}_{1:T}$ to obtain:
   · Marginal likelihood estimate $\hat{Z}^{(m)} = \prod_{t=1}^T \left( \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N L_t^{(i)} \right)$
   · Filtered state trajectory $\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}^{(m)}$
   b. Parameter Update (Metropolis-Hastings):
   · Propose $\boldsymbol{\theta}^* \sim q(\cdot \mid \boldsymbol{\theta}^{(m)})$
   · Run particle filter for $\boldsymbol{\theta}^*$ to obtain $\hat{Z}^*$
   · Accept with probability $\alpha = \min\left(1, \frac{p(\boldsymbol{\theta}^*) \hat{Z}^* q(\boldsymbol{\theta}^{(m)} \mid \boldsymbol{\theta}^*)}{p(\boldsymbol{\theta}^{(m)}) \hat{Z}^{(m)} q(\boldsymbol{\theta}^* \mid \boldsymbol{\theta}^{(m)})}\right)$
   c. Resampling: If effective sample size $< M/2$, resample parameter particles according to their marginal likelihoods.

