Appendix H: Model Predictive Control Formulation

H.1 Safety Barrier Functions

Definition H.1 (Safety Set). The safe set $\mathcal{S} \subset \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{Q}$ is the complement of the unsafe sets $\mathcal{U} = \cup_i \mathcal{U}_i$, where:

· $\mathcal{U}_1 = \{(\mathbf{x}, q) : q = P_2\}$ (plasma quench)
· $\mathcal{U}_2 = \{(\mathbf{x}, q) : T_g(\mathbf{x}) > T_{\text{safe}}\}$ (overheating)
· $\mathcal{U}_3 = \{(\mathbf{x}, q) : q = F_0\}$ (stagnant flow)

Definition H.2 (Barrier Function). A function $B: \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{Q} \times \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} \to \mathbb{R}$ is a control barrier function (CBF) for $\mathcal{U}$ if:

1. $B(\mathbf{x}, q, a) > 0$ for all $(\mathbf{x}, q) \in \mathcal{U}$,
2. $B(\mathbf{x}, q, a) \le 0$ for all $(\mathbf{x}, q) \in \mathcal{S}$,
3. There exists a control $\mathbf{u}$ such that $\tilde{\mathcal{L}} B(\mathbf{x}, q, a; \mathbf{u}) \le -\alpha(B(\mathbf{x}, q, a))$, where $\alpha$ is a class-$\mathcal{K}$ function.

Theorem H.1 (Safety Guarantee). If $B$ is a valid CBF and the control satisfies $\tilde{\mathcal{L}} B \le 0$ at all times, then $\mathbb{P}(X_t \in \mathcal{U} \text{ for some } t) \le B(X_0) / \sup_{\mathcal{U}} B$.

Proof. By Dynkin's formula, $\mathbb{E}[B(X_t)] \le B(X_0)$. Since $B > 0$ on $\mathcal{U}$, the probability of entering $\mathcal{U}$ is bounded. For a rigorous stochastic Lyapunov argument, see Kushner [A18]. ∎

H.2 MPC Optimization Problem

At each time step $t_k$, given state estimate $(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_k, \hat{q}_k, \hat{a}_k)$:

Minimize:
J(\mathbf{u}_{k:k+H-1}) = \sum_{j=0}^{H-1} \ell(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k+j}, \hat{q}_{k+j}, \mathbf{u}_{k+j}) + V_f(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k+H}, \hat{q}_{k+H})

where the stage cost is:

\ell(\mathbf{x}, q, \mathbf{u}) = w_1 (\dot{m}_{O_2}(\mathbf{x}, q) - \dot{m}_{\text{target}})^2 + w_2 \|\mathbf{u} - \mathbf{u}_{\text{nom}}\|^2 + w_3 \max(0, \tilde{\mathcal{L}} B(\mathbf{x}, q, a; \mathbf{u}))

Subject to:

· $\mathbf{x}_{k+j+1} = \Phi_{q_{k+j}}(\mathbf{x}_{k+j}, \Delta t; \mathbf{u}_{k+j})$ (deterministic flow)
· $q_{k+j+1} \sim Q(q_{k+j}, \mathbf{x}_{k+j}; \mathbf{u}_{k+j})$ (mode transitions)
· $\mathbf{u}_{k+j} \in \mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}}$ (admissible controls)
· $\tilde{\mathcal{L}} B_i \le \epsilon_i$ (soft safety constraints)

Terminal Cost: $V_f(\mathbf{x}, q) = \|\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{x}_{\text{ref}}\|_{\mathbf{P}}^2$, where $\mathbf{P}$ solves the Lyapunov equation for the linearized system around the target.

H.3 Numerical Solution via Monte Carlo Tree Search

Due to the stochastic mode transitions, the expected cost $\mathbb{E}[J]$ is approximated by Monte Carlo sampling. At each node, $M$ trajectories are simulated using the reduced-order model. The control sequence is optimized using a derivative-free optimizer (e.g., CMA-ES) due to the non-differentiability introduced by discrete modes.

